+# Code Review Findings: Loyalty.Api
+
+## Дефекты MR
+
+### 1. CRITICAL: app/redeem.py - redeem() function, line 30
+**Problem:** `req.dict()` method doesn't exist in Pydantic v2+  
+**Expected:** `req.model_dump()`  
+**Impact:** AttributeError will crash API on every redeem request  
+**Severity:** critical
+
+---
+
+### 2. HIGH: app/redeem.py - line 11
+**Problem:** `POINT_VALUE = 0.1` is a float, not Decimal  
+**Expected:** `POINT_VALUE = Decimal("0.1")`  
+**Impact:** Float arithmetic causes precision errors in financial calculations (0.1 cannot be precisely represented in binary)  
+**Severity:** high
+
+---
+
+### 3. HIGH: app/redeem.py - line 28
+**Problem:** `int(amount / Decimal(POINT_VALUE))` truncates instead of rounding properly  
+**Example:** amount=10.15, POINT_VALUE=0.1 → 101.5 → 101 points (loss of 0.05 rubles)  
+**Expected:** Use proper rounding (floor, ceil, or round depending on business logic)  
+**Impact:** Financial loss due to truncation errors  
+**Severity:** high
+
+---
+
+### 4. HIGH: app/redeem.py - redeem() function
+**Problem:** Race condition - read (get_member) and write (save_member) operations are not in the same transaction  
+**Scenario:** 
+- Thread A: reads points=100, calculates 100-10=90
+- Thread B: reads points=100, calculates 100-5=95
+- Thread A: saves 90
+- Thread B: saves 95
+- Result: points=95 instead of 85 (lost update)
+
+**Expected:** Use single transaction with row-level locking or optimistic concurrency control  
+**Impact:** Lost update, double spending, data corruption  
+**Severity:** high
+
+---
+
+### 5. MEDIUM: app/redeem.py - line 33
+**Problem:** `valid_until = date.today() + timedelta(days=365)` doesn't match comment "including today"  
+**Expected:** If comment means "365 days including today", should be `date.today() + timedelta(days=364)`  
+**Impact:** Off-by-one error in expiration date calculation  
+**Severity:** medium
+
+---
+
+### 6. MEDIUM: app/repo.py - write_audit() function, line 36
+**Problem:** `json.dumps(payload, default=str)` converts Decimal objects to string representation  
+**Expected:** Use custom JSON encoder or explicit Decimal-to-float/string conversion  
+**Impact:** Audit records will have Decimal as string "10.5" instead of number 10.5, complicating data analysis  
+**Severity:** medium
